    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (SKILL.md row 'Operating company, non-US') + adaptations. Yidu is an operating healthcare data/AI software and services company (AI for Medical big-data platforms for hospitals/governments, Life Sciences RWE/clinical solutions for pharma, Care/Hui Min Bao health insurance management). It is not distressed, not a cash shell and not under a corporate action, so a going-concern FCF model applies. But FY2026 is its FIRST profitable year and the reported RMB78.8m profit is entirely treasury income: operating profit RMB87.8m includes RMB145.4m interest on term deposits / fixed-rate notes (other income note 6) and RMB19.1m other gains (fair-value gains on WMP/swaps). Stripping those, core operating loss is ~RMB-76.6m, core EBITDA after SBC ~RMB-39.9m and pre-SBC core EBITDA ~RMB-14m (-1.7% of revenue), vs ~-35% in FY2025 (admin staff cost cut RMB100m->25m, impairments RMB79m->29m). Hence driver year 1 starts near breakeven, not at the headline profit. Value is therefore dominated by the RMB3.35bn net financial-asset position; the operating business is modelled from components. INTEREST: only RMB1.76m of interest sits in OCF ('interest received'); the RMB97.4m of term-deposit interest is received in INVESTING, so it is already outside reported FCF; last_fcf strips only the 1.76m. The treasury assets carry the stripped income in the bridge. NET CASH (31-Mar-2026, RMB m): cash 664.8 + term deposits 1,392.6 + fixed-rate notes at amortised cost (Goldman/JPM/Citi, mature 2027-30) 1,204.0 + accrued interest 53.5 + FVTPL (WMP, total-return swap, VC fund) 103.3 = 3,418.2, less borrowings 65.0 and leases 6.1. Pledged/restricted deposits (22.4) excluded. Remaining unfunded commitment to YD Capital I fund ~US$26.8m is a cash-to-investment swap at fair value and is not deducted. Market cap at the quote (RMB~2.46bn on 1,004.5m outstanding) is ~0.73x net financial assets: the market is pricing either continued burn, cash misallocation, or a governance/VIE discount on the cash. BUYBACKS: RMB260.0m in FY26 - the flat count is funded.",
